// After "26a. Alpha 3", Garlic finds -#5 in less than 1 second.
// However, Iceberg (the specialize mate-finder) cannot find any forced mate even after 30 seconds.
// The same goes for after "27b. Boar &3"--Garlic finds -#4 in less than 1 second,
// while Iceberg cannot find anything even after 30 seconds.
//
// It's sad that the specialized mate-finder is losing to a general-purpose agent.
// When we build the next mate-finder, I think we need a stronger suite.
// One idea might be to scrape each existing game's last 10 or so plies,
// and see which ones Garlic can find mates for in under 30 seconds.
// Then, we can require the mate-finder candidate to also find mates (in those positions) in under 30 seconds.
// That should be a necessary, but obviously not sufficient acceptance condition.
// It's not sufficient because if the mate-finder can only do what Garlic does, then there's no point.
// The whole point of a mate-finder is to find mates in the 10-20 ply range in under 30 seconds.
//
// Export Date: 2026-08-03

0b. =Rabbit; Horse Ram Beta; Rat Ox Tiger Dragon Horse Monkey Rooster Boar Fish Elephant Squid Frog; Ram
0a. =Dog; Dog Elephant Alpha; Rat Ox Tiger Rabbit Snake Snake Monkey Rooster Boar Fish Squid Frog; Dragon
